<resources>
    <!-- USB-C port > Off. GrapheneOS's text describes Pixels, where Off also
         stops charging. On the FP6, charging runs in the ADSP firmware, so
         Off turns data off and refuses new connections like Charging-only,
         and charging continues. GrapheneOS ships this text in English only,
         so there are no translations to replace. -->
    <string name="usbc_port_off_summary">Turns off USB data on the USB-C port. Charging stays on: this device can’t turn it off, so this works like Charging-only.</string>
</resources>
